{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_006","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"Title: Spinning Bar and a Star-formation Inefficient Repertoire: Turbulence in Hickson Compact Group NGC7674","location_hint":"paragraph 18","char_start":873,"char_end":981,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_007","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"Authors: Diane M. Salim , Katherine Alatalo , Christoph Federrath , Brent Groves , Lisa J. Kewley","location_hint":"paragraph 19","char_start":985,"char_end":1082,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_008","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"View a PDF of the paper titled Spinning Bar and a Star-formation Inefficient Repertoire: Turbulence in Hickson Compact Group NGC7674, by Diane M. Salim and 4 other authors","location_hint":"paragraph 20","char_start":1086,"char_end":1257,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_009","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"Abstract: The physics regulating star formation (SF) in Hickson Compact Groups (HCG) has thus far been difficult to describe, due to their unique kinematic properties.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1271,"char_end":1438,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_010","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"In this study we expand upon previous works to devise a more physically meaningful SF relation able to better encompass the physics of these unique systems.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1439,"char_end":1595,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_011","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"We combine CO(1--0) data from the Combined Array from Research in Millimeter Astronomy (CARMA) to trace the column density of molecular gas $\\Sigma_\\mathrm{gas}$ and deep H$\\alpha$ imaging taken on the Southern Astrophysical Research (SOAR) Telescope tracing $\\Sigma_\\mathrm{SFR}$ to investigate star formation efficiency across face-on HCG, NGC7674.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1596,"char_end":1946,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_012","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"We find a lack of universality in star formation, with two distinct sequences present in the $\\Sigma_\\mathrm{gas}-\\Sigma_\\mathrm{SFR}$ plane; one for inside and one for outside the nucleus.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1947,"char_end":2136,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_013","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"We devise a SF relation based on the multi-freefall nature of gas and the critical density, which itself is dependent on the virial parameter $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{vir}}$, the ratio of turbulent to gravitational energy.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2137,"char_end":2351,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_014","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"We find that our modified SF relation fits the data and describes the physics of this system well with the introduction of a virial parameter of about 5--10 across the galaxy.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2352,"char_end":2527,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_015","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"This $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{vir}}$ leads to an order-of-magnitude reduction in SFR compared to $\\alpha_{\\mathrm{vir}}\\approx 1$ systems.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2528,"char_end":2658,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_67b29d913d85_016","source_id":"src_67b29d913d85","source_hash":"927d49c34c96db77d102a705dbe84868e3be41367431c30746f032d539fdeda3","text":"Astrophysics of Galaxies (astro-ph.GA)","location_hint":"paragraph 25","char_start":2711,"char_end":2749,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:36:36.827Z"}
